The bug occurs when the driver attempts to dereference `txqcqs` and `rxqcqs` entries that may not exist after a reduction in the number of queues. If the number of queues is decreased, the driver may try to access and free queue control queue (qcq) entries that are NULL, leading to a NULL pointer dereference and a page fault.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (lif->txqcqs && lif->txqcqs[i]) {
    lif->txqcqs[i]->flags &= ~IONIC_QCQ_F_INTR;
    ionic_qcq_free(lif, lif->txqcqs[i]);
}
```
```c
if (lif->rxqcqs && lif->rxqcqs[i]) {
    lif->rxqcqs[i]->flags &= ~IONIC_QCQ_F_INTR;
    ionic_qcq_free(lif, lif->rxqcqs[i]);
}
```
Reason:
The fix adds checks to ensure that both the `txqcqs` and `rxqcqs` arrays exist and that the specific qcq entry is not NULL before attempting to dereference and free it. This prevents the driver from dereferencing a NULL pointer, thus avoiding the page fault issue.

